# Saving and rollback
@scenario tutorial_lesson_19
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code normal]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/19_saves_rollback_persistence.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt branches]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Save a slot before selecting a test value. You can reload that slot and run the other branch from exactly the same point.
ginger: At the choices, open Pause and choose {b}Save{/b}. Create a slot, resume, then select A or B. Watch the value printed after the selection.
ginger: A slot captures a particular moment in the route. Save before the choice to test both inputs from the same starting point. Save after the write to check how the resulting state restores.
ginger: The printed result gives you a way to inspect example_value. A restored sprite alone cannot tell you whether the variable and script position came back together.
ginger: Scroll up on the dialogue to roll back one step. Try it after choosing A or B. As you step back, watch for both the earlier line and its earlier variable value.
@label select_value
# region branches
> Set value to A -> select_a
> Set value to B -> select_b
# endregion
> Separate saved state from new input -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label select_a
[set example_value A]
ginger: This branch writes A to {b}example_value{/b}.
[jump display_value]
@label select_b
[set example_value B]
ginger: This branch writes B to {b}example_value{/b}.
@label display_value
[set tutorial_excerpt display]
# region display
narrator: Current value: {b}${example_value}{/b}.
# endregion
ginger: Open Load and select your slot. Choose the other value. The readout should now show that value, and you should still be in this lesson.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Separate saved state from new input -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
ginger: Where should you store a choice that must survive saving and loading?
> In VN state so save and rollback can restore it. -> correct
> Only in the displayed dialogue text. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: A line of text displays the result. Subsequent conditions need a value they can read from VN state.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Store the value in VN state. Check the restored value and the current script location when testing a save.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_19]
[flag tutorial_done_19]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/19_saves_rollback_persistence.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt display]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Create slot Before at the A/B choice. Choose A, advance to the printed value, and save again under a second name. You now have snapshots on opposite sides of the write.
ginger: Load Before and choose B. The next readout should be B. Load the later slot and check the current line and readout before making any new choice.
ginger: Trace that readout back to the assignment on each branch. Both routes use the same output line, so a difference there should come from a different stored value.
ginger: Test rollback separately on the same route. Scroll up or press Page Up to step back through dialogue and inspect when the value changes.
ginger: Scroll-up rollback is customizable. In ~/.jvn/input-bindings.properties, the rollback row lists its controls. Keep MOUSE_WHEEL|0||UP to use scroll up, remove that entry to keep keyboard shortcuts only, or use an empty rollback row to disable all its shortcuts.
ginger: Relaunch the game after editing the profile and repeat the exercise. If you already loaded a profile through Settings, reload Input Profile from disk before relaunching.
@label practice_question
ginger: Which slot lets you choose B without replaying the whole lesson?
> The slot captured before the A/B choice. -> practice_result
> The slot captured on the readout after choosing A. -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: The later slot already passed the choice. Locate the snapshot whose instruction position is on the input you want to repeat.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: The earlier slot restores the decision point. Choosing B then executes its write before the shared readout is evaluated.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
